WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.630
Every learner deserves the chance
to explore the world they live in.

2
00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:09.650
But across Southeast Asia, many
youth face barriers to education.

3
00:00:10.144 --> 00:00:15.350
In Myanmar, about 3.8 million people
are displaced inside their own country.

4
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.450
In Malaysia, refugee children
can't attend government schools.

5
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.910
And in East Asia and the Pacific,

6
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.610
one in three school-age children
had no internet at home.

7
00:00:26.738 --> 00:00:29.750
Where schools are stretched,
lessons often stick to the basics:

8
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.690
reading, maths, and skills for a job.

9
00:00:32.926 --> 00:00:33.926
Those matter.

10
00:00:34.101 --> 00:00:37.310
But there's little room left for
the skills that open up the world:

11
00:00:37.444 --> 00:00:39.980
thinking critically,
communicating with evidence,

12
00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.570
and taking other perspectives.

13
00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:44.330
Research backs this up.

14
00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:45.710
In a Stanford study,

15
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.300
students who learned
history by questioning real

16
00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:51.370
sources grew more in historical thinking,

17
00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:54.810
reading, and knowledge than
students in regular classes.

18
00:00:56.063 --> 00:00:57.610
That's why we built Thinkerwell:

19
00:00:57.747 --> 00:01:00.350
free lessons in social studies and beyond,

20
00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.030
for youth facing barriers to education.

21
00:01:04.036 --> 00:01:06.180
Our first course, Exploring Our World,

22
00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:09.310
has 24 lessons in history, geography,

23
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.270
culture, and civic life, and
every lesson has five steps.

24
00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:14.281
Read.

25
00:01:14.321 --> 00:01:15.110
Write.

26
00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.010
Speak.

27
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:16.940
Watch.

28
00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:17.980
Reflect.

29
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.430
Every reading has a simpler
version and can be read aloud,

30
00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.110
and lessons work offline, in
English and Bahasa Indonesia.

31
00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.130
Thinkerwell doesn't replace teachers.

32
00:01:28.424 --> 00:01:32.150
It lightens their load, with a
ready-made guide for every lesson,

33
00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.310
plus answer keys and printables.

34
00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.850
Our goal is to help
learners ask questions,

35
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.070
grow their critical thinking skills,

36
00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.790
explore diverse perspectives,
and share their own ideas.

37
00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:45.540
Thinkerwell.

38
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.250
Social studies and beyond.

39
00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:49.280
Explore your world.

